    {
      "id": "SHEAVES-RECON-019",
      "source": "sheaves.tex",
      "operations": [
        {
          "line": 1277,
          "old_text": "Hence $A = A \\times_B C$ because $F$ reflects isomorphisms.",
          "replacement_text": "Hence the first projection $p_A : A \\times_B C \\to A$ is an isomorphism because $F$ reflects isomorphisms.",
          "start_byte": 43916,
          "end_byte_exclusive": 43975,
          "old_sha256": "69B6787F65670FFA3D5FB2B32473E5C75871DE9B68A4D754C352F72CE8354794",
          "replacement_sha256": "ECDCA81DF1C276E125F9014F4D2087411047B87D070CB07286E325C117F54AFF",
          "operation_id": "SHEAVES-RECON-019-OP1"
        },
        {
          "line": 1278,
          "old_text": "The result follows.",
          "replacement_text": "Writing $p_C : A \\times_B C \\to C$ for the second projection, set $t = p_C \\circ p_A^{-1}$. The fibre product identity gives $g \\circ t = f$.",
          "start_byte": 43976,
          "end_byte_exclusive": 43995,
          "old_sha256": "BA711694851E9F9B8C242D6AC7989E8FF32677C9F07183C2005A991501828602",
          "replacement_sha256": "D75607B96727986BED54F6A5BD8454E431877B2A1845F5968A5C12043E5CD1D2",
          "operation_id": "SHEAVES-RECON-019-OP2"
        }
      ],
      "producer_occurrences": [
        "OCC-01244"
      ],
      "class": "accepted_missing_clarification",
      "rationale": "Let P=A times_B C with projections p_A and p_C. Since F preserves fibre products, F(p_A) identifies with the projection from pairs (a,c) satisfying F(f)(a)=F(g)(c). The image inclusion gives a c for every a, and injectivity of F(g) makes it unique. Thus F(p_A) is bijective, so reflection of isomorphisms makes p_A invertible. Setting t=p_C composed with p_A inverse gives g composed with t=f by the fibre-product identity. Name this exact isomorphism and factorization explicitly.",
      "adverse_evidence": "The equality signs can already denote these canonical identifications; the report does not refute the factorization theorem. This is a clarification of the morphisms used in the proof, not a new theorem or counterexample.",
      "review_file": "SHEAVES_INTAKE_REVIEW_20260923.json",
      "discovery": null,
      "related_existing_canonical_ids": []
    },
